---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Eagle Mountain - Hardware - Rycode"
  description="Meta's Eagle Mountain, Utah data center: investment raised to more than $3 billion on 14 September 2026, with closed-loop dry cooling."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Hardware · Data center</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Eagle Mountain</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Eagle Mountain is Meta's data center in Utah, where Meta broke ground in 2018. On 14 September 2026 Meta said it is expanding the site and raising its Utah investment to more than $3 billion (<a href="https://datacenters.atmeta.com/2026/09/deepening-our-investment-in-eagle-mountain-utah/">Meta, 14 Sep 2026</a>).</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Key figures</h2>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">Eagle Mountain data center</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Investment in Utah</td><td>More than $3 billion</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ground broken</td><td>2018</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Construction workers at peak</td><td>More than 1,200</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jobs once complete</td><td>More than 300</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clean energy added in Utah</td><td>More than 1.7 GW, plus 600 MWh of batteries</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>MWh, megawatt-hours, measures stored energy: a battery that can deliver one megawatt for one hour.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Cooling</h2>
    <p>Meta says the new buildings use a closed-loop liquid cooling system with dry cooling, so the cooling system uses no water once running. Closed loop means the same liquid circulates again and again; dry cooling means fans, not evaporating water, carry the heat away. See <a href="/ai/hardware/cooling/">Cooling</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">What is not public</h2>
    <p>Meta has not given a power capacity in megawatts or a chip count for Eagle Mountain in this post.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://datacenters.atmeta.com/2026/09/deepening-our-investment-in-eagle-mountain-utah/">Meta, Deepening our investment in Eagle Mountain (14 Sep 2026)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
